/-!
# Single-root authority firewall

This regression keeps only attacks which can change the admitted world:

* pruning the complete actual-event inventory;
* borrowing authority from a sibling field or ledger row;
* promoting a completed field/oracle to an actual atom;
* executing inquiry or U8 payloads outside the fixed root occurrence;
* reintroducing a parallel lifecycle or revision-selection authority.
* activating an arbitrary process state or an uninstalled public face.
* replacing an inquiry macro successor by its old-root micro-successor, or
  preloading a completed table of future query activations.

Historical API spellings live in Git history.  This file guards semantic
boundaries and the current public factorization mouths, not an ever-growing
list of deleted identifiers.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

open SaturationMonoid
open SaturationMonoid.ResponsibilityLifecycle
open SaturationMonoid.ResponsibilityLifecycle.LivingLawEvolution.ConstructiveRoot

/-! ## The active facade exposes one root authority graph -/

